From 8539be92f93739a99662523abb51b6a461b44ebc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arkenoi <6000406+arkenoi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 23:58:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Phase 1A: per-frame timing instrumentation for the
 capture/send path

Splits the frame pipeline into measurable phases so the Phase 1A decision
(does window tracking/enumeration dominate, or repaint/dirty-rect volume?)
is made from data rather than assumption:

  (a) tracking : upd + enu + rem  (UpdateWindowData / AddAllWindows-EnumWindows /
                 removal pass - the per-frame EnumWindows the README TODO targets)
  (b) damage   : drq + dmg        (GetFrameDirtyRects + damage processing)
  (c) send     : snd              (all VCHAN_SEND/VCHAN_SEND_MSG, routed through
                 VchanSendTimed so MSG_CONFIGURE writes are not billed to (a))

Emits one CSV-ish line per frame at LOG_LEVEL_INFO via the agent's existing
rotating logger (no new log file), with QueryPerformanceCounter timings in us,
self-cost calibrated at startup, plus dirty/move rect counts, dirty area and
window count. Also records wak (capture SetEvent -> ProcessNewFrame entry) to
expose scheduler delay on a 4-vCPU HVM.

Move rects are measured explicitly (GetFrameMoveRects into a stack buffer,
before the dirty-rect block per the DXGI contract) to settle the capture.c:441
note. ddaprobe already measured ZERO move rects on the Basic Display Adapter
across an idle run and a 25s window-drag; this confirms it from inside the agent.

Runtime-guarded (QUBES_GUI_PERF env > PerfLog DWORD > compile default): when off
the residue is one predicted-taken branch, so this stays small and upstreamable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 363b38a68371461a3608a3ea7c85e4dbb88611c8)
---
