From e5ea33d32bb0ce8801dcca758ead523302a9d16f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arkenoi <6000406+arkenoi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 01:29:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Phase 2A: event-driven window tracking (SetWinEventHook),
 review fixes applied

Replaces the per-frame AddAllWindows() pass - which re-interrogated all 67
ineligible top-level windows every frame at ~340us each (cross-process
GetWindowText + DwmGetWindowAttribute) - with a dedicated hook thread feeding a
pending-window queue, plus a reject cache and a periodic resync backstop.

Adversarial review found 9 defects; the blocking ones are fixed here:

D1 dropped the "pending resync suppresses the signal" shortcut. It depended on
   an invariant DiscardWindowEvents() breaks, so after seamless off->on every
   event took the suppressed path and window moves silently fell back to
   capture rate.
D2 the reject signature is now sampled BEFORE interrogation. Sampling it after
   could bake in a state change that happened during interrogation, so a
   coalesced EVENT_OBJECT_SHOW would hide the window from dom0 forever -
   defeating the resync in exactly the case it exists for.
D3 the hook thread no longer calls AttachToInputDesktop(): that writes shared
   g_StartWindow/g_SearchWindow unsynchronised (the reject cache now depends on
   them, so a torn read would cache the real Start window as ineligible,
   permanently) and CloseDesktop()s the process-default handle, which MSDN
   forbids and a third caller would double-close. Only the per-thread
   OpenInputDesktop/SetThreadDesktop is done, closing only this thread's handle.
D4 tot now includes tracking done between frames. Otherwise upd+enu exceed tot
   once the hook moves work out of the frame, and the analyzer reports >100%
   shares and negative "unaccounted" - invalidating the very measurement Phase
   2A is judged on.
D6 the admit path consults the reject cache. Events whose effect is visible in
   the cheap signature (LOCATIONCHANGE/STATECHANGE) no longer force
   re-interrogation, while CLOAKED/UNCLOAKED/CREATE/SHOW/HIDE/NAMECHANGE always
   do. Without this an event-noisy ineligible window re-paid the full cost at
   input rate - reinstating exactly what this change removes.
D7 hook-thread death is now logged and drops the resync interval to 150ms, so
   failure degrades to roughly the old cadence instead of 0.5Hz - below par.
D8 a failed ExamineWindow re-requests a resync instead of silently dropping the
   rest of the batch.

Also fixes a pre-existing leak: the old AddWindowsProc malloc'd WINDOW_DATA for
every rejected window and never freed it (~67/frame).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6d4613269339cbfd3e6a33a2e663fe522c4a6faa)
