From 1ce25bef5bf3e861f87be284dbd7a1a3f1ed4453 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arkenoi <6000406+arkenoi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 02:28:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] 2A-chrome: reject only owned click-through layered
 chrome; drop the alpha rule

Rejects the Office 2013+ shadow-strip HWNDs so a compound window stops appearing
in dom0 as several separately-bordered fragments. One conservative rule, all
five clauses required: WS_EX_LAYERED+WS_EX_TRANSPARENT (can never receive a
click), Owner != NULL (unowned top-levels are somebody's real UI), no WS_CAPTION,
no WS_EX_APPWINDOW, and BOTH WS_EX_NOACTIVATE and WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW. Costs nothing
per frame - it reads state GetWindowData() already collects, plus Owner from a
GetWindow(GW_OWNER) call that was already there for the modal check.

Review fixes applied:
- REMOVED the proposed 'alpha == 0 layered window' rule entirely. Windows fades
  menus and tooltips IN from alpha 0, so sampling one as it appears would reject
  AND cache it; SetLayeredWindowAttributes emits no WinEvent, so it would stay
  invisible in dom0 until the next resync. Applied to an already-mapped window it
  turns a transient fade-out into MSG_DESTROY + recreate, losing z-order and
  focus. Its only benefit was cosmetic and it does not even match the Office
  strips, which are VISIBLE shadows with alpha > 0. A missing window is far worse
  than a spurious border. The Alpha plumbing is removed with it.
- NOACTIVATE|TOOLWINDOW tightened from either to BOTH: a comctl32 tooltip is
  owned, toolwindow and can be WS_EX_TRANSPARENT, but generally not NOACTIVATE.
- The reject log demoted to LogVerbose: during a drag each strip is re-examined
  at input rate (rect changes invalidate its cached signature), so LogDebug meant
  hundreds of formatted lines a second with a cross-process class name.
- chromerepro --control canary: dropped WS_BORDER. WS_CAPTION is
  WS_BORDER|WS_DLGFRAME, so the canary was being spared by the caption clause and
  never exercised the WS_EX_TRANSPARENT clause it exists to test.

Cloaked windows need no new rule: GetWindowData already folds DWMWA_CLOAKED into
IsVisible and the predicate rejects !IsVisible first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 580328e1b8b0629ea6ee68e252950bbf5c7d58ea)
---
 gui-agent/main.c | 96 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 gui-agent/main.h |  8 ++++
 2 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

